            <h3>High-Speed vs Regional Trains</h3>
            <p>The United States does not currently have high-speed rail on this cross-regional route. The Silver Meteor is considered a long-distance intercity train with consistent speeds up to 125 mph on certain segments and an average speed of 50 mph overall. While significantly slower than flying, the train offers comfortable seating or private rooms, scenic views, included meals for sleeper passengers, and city-center arrivals, which can save time and hassle compared to airport procedures.</p>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Travel is steady, reliable, and scenic, even without high-speed rail.</li>
                <li>The lack of transfers simplifies planning, especially for first-time long-distance rail travelers.</li>
                <li>Choosing the train over flying allows relaxation, work, or sightseeing during the journey, plus the unique experience of overnight train travel.</li>
                <li>The journey is about the experience, not speed - embrace the slower pace and enjoy the changing landscapes from Piedmont to subtropical Florida.</li>
            </ul>
